# Build context sent to the remote builder.
#
# .env is first for a reason: it holds the CDP API secret and, on this machine,
# a wallet private key. The Dockerfile never COPYs it, so it would not reach the
# image — but without this line it is still uploaded to a third-party builder.
# Secrets belong in `fly secrets set`, never in a build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.npmrc
.dev.vars
*.pem
*secret*.txt
*api*.txt
cdp_wallet_secret.txt
cdp_api_key.json

# Reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile; uploading ~120MB of it makes
# every deploy slow and changes nothing.
**/node_modules

# Payment state and logs are machine-local, and the ledger is mounted at /data.
.used-tx.log
*.log

# Not part of the API service.
mcp-client
test
docs
.wrangler
.claude
.obsidian
*.mcpb

# Build outputs, regenerated in the image. `**/` because a bare name matches
# only at the context root, which let apify-actor/dist ship a stale build.
**/dist

# Repository metadata the build does not need.
.git
.github
.gitignore
*.md
!README.md
